{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20079",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.69,
      "end_seconds": 9.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.44,
      "text": "Doctor, the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.71,
      "end_seconds": 15.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Thanks. Hello, come in, sit down. What brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 21.41,
      "end_seconds": 25.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 28.08,
      "end_seconds": 32.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "She's been having been feeling dizzy when I stand up, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.39,
      "end_seconds": 37.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.35,
      "end_seconds": 40.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Around three days, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 42.26,
      "end_seconds": 47.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Okay, so I think it's been nearer five days, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.84,
      "end_seconds": 53.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly three to five days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.15,
      "end_seconds": 56.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Ah, yes, somewhere around that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.37,
      "end_seconds": 61.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.01,
      "end_seconds": 69.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.41,
      "end_seconds": 75.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.28,
      "end_seconds": 77.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "It's moderate, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.57,
      "end_seconds": 80.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "What brings it on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.11,
      "end_seconds": 84.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "It's worse with standing up quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.05,
      "end_seconds": 91.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 91.49,
      "end_seconds": 98.86,
      "duration_seconds": 7.37,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.94,
      "end_seconds": 106.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on. Have you been feeling weak?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.53,
      "end_seconds": 112.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.96,
      "end_seconds": 115.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.38,
      "end_seconds": 120.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.84,
      "end_seconds": 140.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "A few quick ones: palpitations, slurred speech or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.73,
      "end_seconds": 155.11,
      "duration_seconds": 13.38,
      "text": "No, no palpitations, no slurred speech, no fainting. I did have nearly blacking out at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.13,
      "end_seconds": 160.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "A few quick ones: chest pain or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.48,
      "end_seconds": 163.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.27,
      "end_seconds": 166.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Have you had any black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.95,
      "end_seconds": 170.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "No. No black stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.95,
      "end_seconds": 173.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.69,
      "end_seconds": 177.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.55,
      "end_seconds": 191.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.41,
      "end_seconds": 196.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.89,
      "end_seconds": 199.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "So, what's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.02,
      "end_seconds": 204.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.2,
      "end_seconds": 210.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.09,
      "end_seconds": 225.23,
      "duration_seconds": 13.14,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.75,
      "end_seconds": 228.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.83,
      "end_seconds": 233.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "I had an operation for a hernia last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.4,
      "end_seconds": 238.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.15,
      "end_seconds": 241.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.02,
      "end_seconds": 248.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.91,
      "end_seconds": 256.99,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a round yellow one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.24,
      "end_seconds": 260.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.58,
      "end_seconds": 283.03,
      "duration_seconds": 21.45,
      "text": "For my pressure, I believe. My son sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Escitalopram. I take it 10 milligrams, once a day. I take propranolol, 40 milligrams, twice a day for the migraine prevention."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 284.84,
      "end_seconds": 291.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "That's what's prescribed, but I'm not sure she takes it every day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.74,
      "end_seconds": 297.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "I used to take sumatriptan, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.05,
      "end_seconds": 304.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Right, what about your medical history? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.29,
      "end_seconds": 309.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.14,
      "end_seconds": 312.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "And besides that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.04,
      "end_seconds": 316.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Yes, anxiety. I've had migraines, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.29,
      "end_seconds": 324.84,
      "duration_seconds": 7.55,
      "text": "Right, so high blood pressure and migraines are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 325.54,
      "end_seconds": 335.94,
      "duration_seconds": 10.4,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Heart rate 107, respiratory rate 19, temp 36.4 degrees. Blood pressure 95 over 56, oxygen saturation is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.74,
      "end_seconds": 337.44,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.7,
      "end_seconds": 342.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.86,
      "end_seconds": 345.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.66,
      "end_seconds": 364.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal and the chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.06,
      "end_seconds": 366.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.34,
      "end_seconds": 384.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Your blood pressure drops when you stand, from the lying reading to standing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.62,
      "end_seconds": 410.14,
      "duration_seconds": 20.52,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Okay, thinking it through, this is probably postural low blood pressure, possibly related to medicines or dehydration. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. Dehydration is still possible. An abnormal heart rhythm is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 411.75,
      "end_seconds": 415.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 416.76,
      "end_seconds": 446.27,
      "duration_seconds": 29.51,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's postural low blood pressure, possibly related to medicines or dehydration, and we'll know more once the a lying and standing blood pressure check is back. I want a lying and standing blood pressure check done, that's for dizziness. I'd like to arrange an ECG for dizziness. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 448.23,
      "end_seconds": 460.32,
      "duration_seconds": 12.09,
      "text": "Get up slowly from lying and sitting, and keep drinking fluids through the day. I'll want another look after the results are back. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 461.5,
      "end_seconds": 464.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 466.36,
      "end_seconds": 468.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}